00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:28.020
In trade developments, Vietnam and the United States have agreed to increase cooperation targeting illegal transshipment and trade fraud.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.240
The arrangement focuses on customs verification and supply chain monitoring.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:43.880
Officials from both countries sign the cooperation framework in recent days. The agreement includes provisions for sharing shipment data and conducting joint reviews.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:51.760
US trade officials describe the step as a way to ensure compliance with existing agreements and protect domestic industries.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:58.820
Vietnamese authorities frame the partnership as support for legitimate exporters while addressing enforcement gaps.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:10.720
Both sides accept that certain goods have been rerouted to evade tariffs. The difference lies in how quickly new verification systems can be implemented without disrupting normal commerce.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.020
Trade volume between the two countries has grown substantially in recent years.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:27.280
Now, some progress worth knowing about. Vietnam and the United States have begun coordinated customs checks and information sharing aimed at stopping illegal transshipment.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:34.160
